# Where this box copies its database while it runs a hall (a Litestream replica).
#
# Only for a box paired with a hall in the cloud that has a spare box standing by.
# The cloud already gets every move within seconds; the replica is a second copy,
# about once a second, in a store of your own (MinIO on a server in the hall or at
# home, an S3 bucket, SFTP). A spare that takes over reads it too, and loses
# seconds, not whatever the line to the cloud had not carried yet.
#
# To use it: copy this file to "alnasl-replica.txt" (same folder, no .example),
# fill in the lines below, and boot the Pi. At boot the box reads the file, keeps
# the settings on its data partition where only the system can read them, and
# DELETES the file so the key does not stay on the card. Give every box of the
# hall, the spare too, the same file: each writes under its own name in the store
# and the spare reads the one that ran the hall.
#
# A file whose first line is "off" removes the settings again.
# Lines starting with # are ignored. No quotes, no spaces in the values.

# The store and a folder in it (s3://, sftp://, gs://, abs:// or file:///):
ALNASL_TAKEOVER_REPLICA=s3://alnasl-replicas/my-hall
# For MinIO or another S3-compatible store that is not Amazon's, its address:
#ALNASL_TAKEOVER_REPLICA_ENDPOINT=http://192.168.1.20:9000
#ALNASL_TAKEOVER_REPLICA_REGION=us-east-1
# A key that may write to that bucket, and only that one:
LITESTREAM_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
LITESTREAM_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
